# Dependencies & build output — reinstalled / rebuilt inside the image
#
# `**/` is load-bearing, not tidiness: a .dockerignore pattern with no `**` is
# anchored at the context root, so a bare `node_modules/` left every
# `packages/*/node_modules` in the build context. pnpm fills those with symlinks
# — on Windows, junctions — and the remote builder's tar cannot classify one:
# `archive/tar: unknown file mode ?rwxr-xr-x`, and the deploy dies at ~36 MB of
# context transfer with nothing pointing at the cause (2026-08-13). Nested
# installs only appeared once the repo grew workspace packages.
**/node_modules/
# `**/` again, for the same reason and one more: a .dockerignore pattern with no
# `**` is anchored at the context root, so the bare forms below stopped matching
# the moment the Next project moved to apps/web — `.next/` would have shipped a
# local dev build into the image (2026-08-12).
**/.next/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/next-env.d.ts

# Secrets & runtime data — never bake into the image
.env
.env.*
data/

# Caches, VCS, local tooling
.git
.github
# Agent-session state; worktrees under here carry full checkouts + pnpm
# junctions that break the remote builder's tar (deploy failure 2026-07-27)
.claude/
**/.turbo/
**/.vitest-cache/
**/coverage/
.vscode
.idea
scratchpad/
.codex/
scripts/

# Local-only UI/QA artifacts — Playwright scratch.
.playwright-mcp/

# Eval/dev-task render output (gitignored; the designated destination for all
# graded evidence). Never referenced by the app, and at ~70 MB it dominated the
# build context.
eval-images/

# drizzle-kit's per-migration schema snapshots are generate-time diff inputs
# only (~24 MB). The release-time migrator (scripts/db-migrate.ts →
# drizzle-orm's migrate()) reads meta/_journal.json and the .sql files, never
# the snapshots — so those two stay in the context.
drizzle/meta/*_snapshot.json

# The Vesper-owned SDXL renderer: a separate Cog/ComfyUI image built and pushed
# to Replicate on its own, never part of the web app. The Dockerfile's blanket
# `COPY . .` would otherwise ship its Python, its Cog definition and its workflow
# snapshots into the Fly image, where nothing can run them.
packages/image-sd/deployment/

# Documentation is not needed on the web app, only the repo
docs/

